    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "Large models (70B+, MoE like Kimi-K2.6) can quickly exhaust host memory and make the node unresponsive over SSH."
  }, {
    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "**Rules:**"
  }, {
    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "Always set `resources.requests` and `resources.limits` for both CPU and memory, not just GPU."
  }, {
    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "Use `restartPolicy: OnFailure` with `backoffLimit: 1` for heavy jobs."
  }, {
    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "Prefer Jobs over Deployments for one-shot or long-running inference servers that you control explicitly."
  }, {
    "heading": "resource-management-is-critical",
    "content": "Never use `imagePullPolicy: Always` on multi-hundred-GB images."
  }, {
    "heading": "preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot",
    "content": "We do **not** use Deployments with high replica counts for heavy models."
  }, {
    "heading": "preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot",
    "content": "We do **not** use `restartPolicy: Always` for the main inference container."
  }, {
    "heading": "preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot",
    "content": "Workloads are started manually via `scripts/manage.sh`."
  }, {
    "heading": "preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot",
    "content": "After reboot you must explicitly re-deploy."
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "No inter-node NCCL. Local multi-GPU (if advertised) uses SHM/P2P, and the `highspeed`\ninventory group is ignored."
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "**2-node pair (dual \\~400G aggregate):** existing Jobs and `group_vars` `highspeed_*` /\n`nccl_env` are **reference for a pair**. Typical env:"
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "**3-node QSFP ring (200 Gb/s per pair, triangle mesh):** used by Mode B (`glm-5.3-flash`)\nand Mode C (`deepseek-v4.1-flash`). OOB/Gloo on 10GbE (often `enP7s7`); payload on all\nfour CX-7 RoCE devices; `NCCL_NET_PLUGIN=none`. Do **not** copy the 2-node pair vars onto\nthat ring. Confirm names with `ibdev2netdev`. See LiteLLM rounded stack."
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "**4 / 5-node CRS804 switch:** each node sees **one** RoCE link — one full port per node\n(400G) for 4 nodes, or three full ports plus one port split into `sfpplus4a` / `sfpplus4b`\n(two 200G lanes) for 5. Every link is its own /24 (192.168.110–114, MTU 9000) from the\ngenerated per-node netplan. `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` stays the management NIC; the payload\nrides the single RoCE HCA (`NCCL_IB_HCA` from live `ibdev2netdev` names per node). Heavy\nJobs use `hostNetwork: true` — do not assume the 2-node pair `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` list is\ncomplete. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "If NCCL payload falls back to the management network, performance will be terrible."
  }, {
    "heading": "high-speed-interconnect",
    "content": "Full fabric env: Interconnect & NCCL."
  }, {
    "heading": "hostnetwork-and-hostipc",
    "content": "**Omitted** (default false) on kimi / kimi-test and several 1-GPU vLLM Jobs — isolation; NCCL IFNAME still set in env."
  }, {
    "heading": "hostnetwork-and-hostipc",
    "content": "**`hostNetwork: true`** on Ray, GLM-5.2, Qwen 397B, Mode B/C — ranks need the fabric NICs."
  }, {
    "heading": "hostnetwork-and-hostipc",
    "content": "**`hostIPC: true`** on GLM RPC and Mode B/C ring Jobs — shared memory for TP."
  }, {
    "heading": "hostnetwork-and-hostipc",
    "content": "Do not add hostNetwork to a Job “for luck”; follow the workload YAML."
  }, {
    "heading": "ple-mmap-qwen38-flash-next",
    "content": "Mode A `qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4` requires PLE mmap (weights mapped, not fully resident). Prefix caching off. Start `max-model-len` 65536. See LiteLLM rounded stack."
  }, {
    "heading": "ple-mmap-qwen38-flash-next",
    "content": "Verify interfaces on the nodes:"
  }, {
    "heading": "gpu-operator-on-k3s",
    "content": "The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"
  }, {
    "heading": "gpu-operator-on-k3s",
    "content": "Use a recent version (v24.x+ recommended)."
  }, {
    "heading": "gpu-operator-on-k3s",
    "content": "The driver container may take several minutes to load after first boot."
  }, {
    "heading": "gpu-operator-on-k3s",
    "content": "On reboot, wait for `nvidia-smi` to succeed on both nodes before deploying heavy workloads."
  }, {
    "heading": "gpu-operator-on-k3s",
    "content": "MIG is supported but requires explicit configuration in the ClusterPolicy."
  }, {
    "heading": "dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing",
    "content": "A single GB10 exposes **one** physical GPU. To schedule two inference Jobs concurrently (e.g. Qwen3.6 dual):"
  }, {
    "heading": "dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing",
    "content": "Apply `k8s/base/gpu-time-slicing` (`replicas: 2`)."
  }, {
    "heading": "dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing",
    "content": "Point the device plugin at that ConfigMap (`gpu_time_slicing_enabled: true` in Ansible, or helm upgrade)."
  }, {
    "heading": "dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing",
    "content": "Split memory with `--gpu-memory-utilization` (\\~0.38 each). Never run two processes at 0.9 util."
  }, {
    "heading": "dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing",
    "content": "See qwen36-dual-stack.md."
  }, {
    "heading": "blackwell-nvfp4-kernels",
    "content": "On DGX Spark, set `CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a`. For MoE NVFP4, use `--moe-backend flashinfer_b12x` or inference can be \\~2–2.5× slower (Marlin fallback)."
  }, {
    "heading": "stability-tips",
    "content": "Reserve headroom: leave at least 10-20% of host RAM and CPU free for the system + K3s."
  }, {
    "heading": "stability-tips",
    "content": "Use node affinity so that heavy inference prefers specific nodes if needed."
  }, {
    "heading": "stability-tips",
    "content": "Monitor with:"
  }, {
    "heading": "stability-tips",
    "content": "If SSH becomes laggy, the node is likely OOMing. Hard power cycle may be required in extreme cases."
  }, {
    "heading": "stability-tips",
    "content": "Consider using `limit` equal to `request` for memory to get OOMKilled instead of silent swapping."
  }, {
