  }, {
    "heading": "patch-and-reboot",
    "content": "Large Jobs can exhaust host memory and make SSH unusable. `restartPolicy: OnFailure` will **not** bring them back — you must start again — but a reboot *during* a 90Gi+ Job can still hang the node."
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "From the workstation:"
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "Confirm `kubectl get pods -n {{NAMESPACE}}` is empty (or Completed and deleted)."
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "Optional: `kubectl drain <node> --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data` for worker OS patches. Drain does **not** replace step 1 for Jobs that already occupy unified memory."
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "Patch OS packages on the node (vendor docs). For GPU Operator, re-run `bazelisk run //ansible:gpu-operator -- -i inventory/hosts.ini` **after** nodes are up, not during a hung driver compile with inference running."
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "Reboot **workers first** (spark1+), then spark0. 1-node: just spark0 after stop."
  }, {
    "heading": "sequence",
    "content": "Use IPMI/iDRAC/console if SSH is already degraded."
  }, {
    "heading": "after-reboot",
    "content": "Heavy profiles stay off until you start them. That is the safety property."
  }, {
    "heading": "after-reboot",
    "content": "Driver containers can take 5–15+ minutes. Watch `kubectl get pods -n gpu-operator -w` before starting Jobs."
  }],
