    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Manage GPU graphics clocks on DGX Spark (Blackwell GB10) for thermal stability."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "**Intent**: GB10 has no user-controllable power limit or fan curve on DGX Spark\n(`nvidia-smi -pl` and fan speed return N/A). The only operator-accessible actuator\nis graphics clock locking via `nvidia-smi -lgc`. Range lock (default 300–2200 MHz)\ncaps peak clocks to avoid sustained 78–88°C temps and thermal shutdowns during\nlong-running inference, with near-zero impact on memory-bound MoE workloads."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "**Idempotency** (core of the utility pattern):"
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "`status` reports configured lock range, telemetry, and health classification."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "`run` is a no-op when the configured lock range already matches targets."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Service install is idempotent (only rewrites unit if content differs)."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "**Safety**:"
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Never touches ai-inference namespace workloads."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Requires nvidia-smi; mutation verbs require root (or passwordless sudo)."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Respects the lab's GPU Operator + nvidia-persistenced."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Detects PD-degraded states (513–650 MHz / \\~15W) and advises power-cycle."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Usage (CLI):"
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Env overrides: CLOCK\\_FLOOR\\_MHZ, CLOCK\\_CEILING\\_MHZ (TARGET\\_CLOCK\\_MHZ aliases ceiling),\nTHERMAL\\_WARN\\_C, THERMAL\\_HOT\\_C, PD\\_\\* thresholds."
  }, {
    "heading": "spark-clock",
    "content": "Dashboard integration: The UI will call status --json and run/reset subcommands."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Safely perform full system + firmware update on DGX Spark nodes and prepare for reboot."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "**Intent**: Keep base OS (apt dist-upgrade) and firmware (fwupdmgr) current.\nCRITICAL LAB SAFETY: Never reboot while heavy inference workloads are running.\nAlways stop jobs first (manage.sh stop) and verify clean before reboot."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "**Idempotency** (per utility pattern):"
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "status reports exactly what is pending and whether safe to proceed."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "run is safe to repeat (checks state; only acts on pending items)."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Reboot step is gated and only suggested when safe."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "**Safety**:"
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Refuses destructive actions (reboot path) if active jobs in ai-inference."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Respects reboot-safety golden rule."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Must integrate with manage.sh stop before any reboot."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Uses shared helpers for logging and cluster checks."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "Dashboard will call status --json and run."
  }, {
    "heading": "system-update",
    "content": "See reboot-safety.md and AGENTS for mandatory pre-reboot steps."
  }, {
