    "heading": "dgx-spark-hardware-reference",
    "content": "Kubelet reservations (Ansible `k3s_kubelet_reserved_args`): `system-reserved=cpu=4,memory=64Gi` + `kube-reserved=cpu=2,memory=8Gi` per node. Resource Guard adds **15% / 24Gi minimum headroom per node** (`config/resource-policy.yaml`): `max(24Gi, 15% of allocatable)`. That floor is **not** a second 64Gi tax after kubelet. Host hang protection is kubelet `system-reserved` (if actually applied) plus MemAvailable soak. Live nodes already schedule 95Gi Jobs, so the documented 64Gi+8Gi kubelet args may not be applied as written — measure allocatable before changing Ansible."
