    "heading": "6-shell-scripts",
    "content": "This section is the lab’s **adapted professional Bash style guide**. It synthesizes Google’s Shell Style Guide, ShellCheck, shfmt, and bats-core practice, tailored to Bazel, kcov, and the generated shell reference."
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Principle"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Lab practice"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Readability first**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Prefer clarity over clever one-liners"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Small, focused functions**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "One responsibility; extract aggressively"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Fail fast and loudly**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "`set -euo pipefail` on entry scripts; never continue in a broken state"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Explicit over implicit**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Quote expansions; name locals; document public APIs"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Testable by design**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Libs are sourceable; entry scripts use thin `main` + source guards"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**ShellCheck is mandatory**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "Warnings are defects until fixed or justified with a comment"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Consistency**"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "shfmt + this section beat personal taste"
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**When to use Bash:** orchestration, thin wrappers, cluster ops (`manage.sh`, utilities). Prefer Python (or another language) when a *new* piece needs complex data structures, non-trivial algorithms, or would be hard to unit-test in shell."
  }, {
    "heading": "philosophy",
    "content": "**Lab exception (scale):** modular domain libraries under `scripts/lib/` may exceed \\~100 lines because they are the operational surface. That is intentional—do not grow a single file with spaghetti; split domains instead. Do **not** rewrite `manage.sh` to Python without an explicit project decision."
  }, {
    "heading": "baseline-entry-scripts",
    "content": "Every **executable** entry script starts with:"
  }, {
    "heading": "baseline-entry-scripts",
    "content": "Prefer `#!/usr/bin/env bash` (portability) over Google’s `#!/bin/bash`."
  }, {
    "heading": "baseline-entry-scripts",
    "content": "Optional: `set -Eeuo pipefail` when you install an `ERR` trap that must inherit into functions."
  }, {
    "heading": "baseline-entry-scripts",
    "content": "Optional: `IFS=$'\\n\\t'` only when the script benefits; do not change IFS globally in libs without care."
  }, {
    "heading": "baseline-entry-scripts",
